hypothetical question for you  what if frogs ruled the earth  not just in terms of numbers but in  terms of their position in the ecosystem  amphitera is a speculative biology  project by the talented artist and  writer roxy valdez which imagines the  incredible and surreal forms frogs might  achieve if given the perfect environment  to evolve while the world of amphitera  often looks like an alien planet the  artist imagines it's actually an  alternate timeline of earth where subtly  different climatic conditions led to  early amphibians out-competing the first  dinosaurs in proto-mammals what  creatures will develop and thrive in  this drastically different history  for this entry into the archive we'll be  exploring the fascinating possibilities  of the amphitera project and remember to  support roxy valdez on patreon using the  links below if you're a fan of this  project  now let's leap back  252 million years and begin our tour  through the timeline of amphitera  our epic tale of frog ascendancy begins  in the early triassic with the oldest  member of the frog lineage the  diminutive triadobatracus this amphibian  is present in our timeline as well but  in the alternate world of amphitera the  wetter damper conditions will lead  triadobatracus to be better suited for  the period than early synapsids and  reptiles as a result its descendants  will rise to the top of this primordial  earth  by the late triassic in what is now  nigeria the common eofrog has emerged  from the triada petrakus and represents  the first major deviation from our world  brought on by the ideal conditions of  this alternate timeline the eofrog is  essentially just a big frog but over  many eons it will provide the anatomical  basis for the most significant species  of this alternate reality the reign of  the amphibians has now begun  by the early jurassic the descendants of  the eofrog have evolved to fill various  major niches across the ecosystems of  the world  in the marshy plains an effective  predator has emerged in the form of the  amusingly named greater moist boy while  these life forms have a comical  appearance the advance they represent is  tremendous having brought their limbs  under their body to be taller and faster  than their competition  the moist boy also possesses an enlarged  clavicular ring which essentially  functions like a rib cage and help  support their growing weight many of the  most successful predators of the future  will branch off from this design  in the rain forest of what is now  northern africa the marbled snap apple  perches on a branch this early tree  dweller has evolved a creeping  unpredictable form of movement  convergent with our timeline's  chameleons and will serve as the  foundation for various unusual offshoots  already it is becoming more sedentary a  lifestyle that will continue until it  reaches truly extreme levels  in the forest of what is now eastern  africa another major tree climbing  species has emerged in the lanky frogget  while they still spend some time on the  forest floor these thin long-legged  organisms are expert climbers patiently  navigating from branch to branch even  more than the snap apple the froggit's  descendants will be the champions of the  world's canopies  and the last major niche filled is that  of the grazing herbivore which is  currently occupied by the lowland dogus  these herd-dwelling lifeforms are the  cousins of the greater moist boy and  have similarly made the critical  advancement of raising their frame off  the ground a wide range of future  herbivorous megafauna will owe their  evolutionary ancestry to the dogus as  the various eofrog descendants continue  to diversify and expand in number  on the dry plains of the cretaceous  period a mighty predator comes to rule  the bull pronks are the descendants of  the greater moist boy and have become  efficient pack predators they hunt  grazing animals in coordinated prides  much like lions in our modern day  to communicate while on patrol the bull  pronks can raise and lower their tails  like signal flags and even flush them  with color  these tales are actually a retained  trait from their tadpole stage showing  these lifeforms have had to get creative  to take over niches typically  unassociated with amphibians  and speaking of getting creative in the  misty rainforests of the north the  mottled sucker lump is a creature whose  specialized lifestyle has caused a  tremendous shift in its body plan even  more than their ancestors the marbled  snap apples these animals are incredibly  inactive with some spending their entire  adult life rooted to a single branch  like an amphibious barnacle as with our  timeline's flatfish their anatomy seems  absurd yet is actually perfectly suited  for their methods of survival the sucker  lumps lifestyle requires few calories so  they can subsist on insects that come  into range of their projectile tongue  and with their characteristic mottled  coloring they can hide effectively from  their prey until it's too late  and further along into the cretaceous  and even stranger variant of the sucker  lump will emerge under the waves the  tropical frondal can be found nestled in  underwater shallows and has a truly  bizarre lifestyle beginning as a free  swimming tadpole once they mature they  never develop limbs becoming completely  stationary filter feeders this lifestyle  requires very little brain power so like  the soft-bodied sea squirts of our  timeline the tropical frondal shockingly  digests most of their brains upon  reaching adulthood repurposing the  valuable proteins elsewhere the  frondal's most characteristic adult  feature is their highly derived tongue  which has evolved sticky branches to  catch the planktonic organisms the  frontal survives on at this point in the  timeline some creatures have clearly  become unrecognizable as amphibians  and high in the treetops around the same  period a frog with an equally bizarre  body plan makes its home the tree frixel  is the descendant of the lanky frogget  the other tree-dwelling specialists that  emerged alongside the snap apple the  tree frixel is even better adapted for  the trees however with a body plan that  at first seems implausibly awkward but  makes perfect sense when the tree friczl  is in its element like our primates the  tree frixl swings through the canopy  above with their hind limbs perfectly  positioned to navigate from branch to  branch as this biomechanical  visualization illustrates as a result  the tree frictions have developed thumb  like digits in a general rise in  cognitive ability given time they may  give rise to something truly special  one relative of the frixel will take a  very different path than its tree  climbing cousins in the force of our  timeline central america you might spot  a gliding aloo thus far in the  infibiteren timeline amphibians have yet  to conquer the skies in the way our  birds or bats have as the ectothermic  low metabolism bodies of amphibians  aren't well equipped for the rigors of  powered flight but the aloo has found a  loophole to hunt it climbs up trees and  uses eyes rotated almost to the back of  its head to calculate the distance of  its prey once a target is locked the elu  leaps back first towards the forest  floor using primitive wings in a  specialized sack that inflates to  provide drag to slow its descent as  bizarre as the alu strategy might seem  it is not unlike the early dinosaurs  like archaeopteryx in our own timeline  that achieved flight the future may yet  hold skies dominated by the eluz  curiously inverted descendants  speaking of curious descendants at the  very end of the cretaceous period the  arid grasslands will give rise to a  creature so bizarre it's at first  difficult to comprehend  this is an inhabited lord a slow bulky  herbivore that is the descendant of the  lowland dogus at a glance the  slow-moving lords might seem vulnerable  to predation but the lorge has its own  private security in the form of the  colonial gobelins a species that have  evolved to live within the lord's hump  the tiny goblins are actually another  branch of the banded sucker lump's  unusual family tree and they've  developed a close symbiotic relationship  with their living nests at the first  sign of danger the goblin horde will  exit the lords and swarm an attacker  until it backs off it's an effective  strategy yet this highly specialized  pairing won't have many offshoots going  forward in a changing world  get another descendant of the lowland  dogus will continue on upon the cold  tundra of the early tertiary period one  amphibian has found an ingenious way to  survive the cold the foaming squander  lives farther north than most amphibian  megafauna can exist yet the squander  stays warm thanks to its eponymous foam  specialized pores on the squander's back  produce a thick towering covering of  insulating foam this foam is similar to  the mucous coating some frogs in our  timeline produce to keep their skin  moist the squander's foam is unique  however as it traps heat within its  structure allowing the squander to roam  the polar reaches with this clever  adaptation descendants of the squander  will be well equipped for the cooling  climate  to the south another species that will  have many successful descendants  dominates the dry step  the stepfragon is a carnivorous behemoth  distantly related to the nimble pack  hunting plane's bullprong now highly  territorial the massive steppe fragon no  longer has a need for a pack hunting all  on its own  but the stepfragon is actually an  omnivore with a lifestyle that could be  compared to a bear gorging itself to  build fat for winter hibernation as the  planet continues to cool the fragons  will endure and will diversify in  unexpected ways  but one creature whose fate is more  mysterious inhabits the trees of  temperate environments high in the  canopy the astonishing freepole live in  elevated wooden villages a descendant of  the tree frixel freeple have achieved a  level of intelligence roughly analogous  to a human like male frigate birds under  their chin freepl have a highly  developed goal or sac for communication  but frequent communication is highly  complex with their language almost  comparable to a curious form of morris  code even more curiously it seems the  freeple vanished from the infibiteren  timeline several million years after  their evolution what fate befilled these  enigmatic creatures did they die out or  given time reach a level of advancement  that allowed for a different kind of  exit we have no way to say for sure but  no matter the nature of their departure  the freeple's absence makes room for  even stranger  species by the late tertiary an isolated  island environment has given rise to a  stunning life-form the splendid fragon  is a descendant of the steppe fragon  that has become a peaceful herbivore  spending its day wading through swampy  jungles on graceful stilt-like legs with  a vibrant coloring a splendid fragon  silently picking their way through their  island home would likely be a  magnificent sight they feed on mushrooms  that grow in this region in abundance  foregoing the omnivorous lifestyle of  their ancestor  on the mainland however another fragon  descendant has taken the opposite path  the catastrophic fragon is the largest  land-dwelling carnivore the world of  amphitera has ever seen the catastrophic  fragon's rotund anatomy might seem  surprising at a glance as it almost  looks too bulky to be able to stand yet  examining the animal skeleton the fragon  center of gravity is a clavicular ring  that began over developing all the way  back in the greater moist boy this ring  acts as the linchpin to the fragon's  massive bulk while the catastrophic  fragon's reign is amazing it's also  rather short an impending drop in  temperature will cause the age of the  fragon to end prematurely  yet one type of fragon already well  adapted to the cold will live on the  arctic fragon thrives into the late  tertiary protected from the cold thanks  to layers of blubber and a thick hide  its most unique adaptation to stay warm  however is the thick coating of fur on  its underside  these hairs are actually dermal  palpillae tubes of skin and fatty tissue  that trap warm air against the fragon's  body much like fur  and since the amphiteren ice age is  imagined to be less severe than our own  the arctic fragons have all they need to  continue to thrive  but there are other ways of surviving  the cold a short distance south the eon  toad are a species with a very different  method of enduring the long winter  months the eon toad is actually a  descendant of the foaming squander that  has traded its foaming coat for  something even stranger eon toads enter  a state of hibernation that can last  multiple years enduring periods of minor  freezing and unfreezing as it waits for  the perfect spring to become active  again while this type of cold protection  is rarely seen in an animal some plants  contain cryo-protectors that stop their  cells from lethal shrinkage while they  allow themselves to be frozen solid for  long periods  and on the subject of plants the eon  toad will often wake to find many types  of vegetation have grown over its body  which can be harmful if left unchecked  and in the same region the final species  of this timeline can be found which  serve as an example of just how alien  the fauna of amphitera can be  the foaming troggle folk are another  descendant of the foaming squander which  are quite a bit smaller than their  ancestors  incredibly trouble folk live in villages  constructed from their characteristic  foam which frees into solid structures  due to the cold they're also highly  communal sculpting the foam on the  bodies of family members into regionally  distinct styles this social grooming  behavior is not unlike that of certain  primates in our timeline and shows an  emerging intelligence  indeed certain communities of trouble  folk have begun cultivating edible  fungus within their nest demonstrating  the beginnings of agriculture like the  fruit before them the troglo folks may  rise to incredible heights  over the course of this journey we've  seen pseudo-frogs rise and fall evolve  incredible adaptations and fulfill  unexpected niches but now we must return  to our own timeline where frogs though  not quite as abundant are still quite  wonderful if you enjoyed learning about  amphitera as much as i did you can  support roxy valdez on patreon and  social media using the links in the  description  and as always thanks for watching if you  enjoyed this entry please lend your  support and like subscribe and hit the  notification icon to stay up to date on  all things curious see you in the next  video  you

